<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine Central Bank reserves detailed.</title>
<headline>Argentine Central Bank reserves detailed.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Argentine Central Bank Wednesday released the following international reserve and currency liability data, in millions:</p>
<p>*A = International reserves (gold, currency, securities,</p>
<p>including repos and reverse repos).</p>
<p>B = Liquidity requirements.</p>
<p>C = International reserves in the financial system.</p>
<p>*D = Monetary base.</p>
<p>E = Currency liabilities.</p>
<p>F = Net repurchase tender agreements.</p>
<p>G = Bank liquidity paper.</p>
<p>H = Financial liabilities.</p>
<p>  Date	*A*   *B*    *C*    *D*    *E*   *F*   *G*    *H*</p>
<p>  Nov 28  19,301 3,762 23,063 11,908 11,910 5,385   571 17,883</p>
<p>  Nov 29  19,309 3,497 22,806 12,062 12,064 5,203   575 17,867</p>
<p>  Dec 02  19,104 4,137 23,241 12,218 12,236 5,490     0 17,769</p>
<p>  Dec 03  19,136 4,230 23,366 12,375 12,393 5,200     0 17,635</p>
<p>  Dec 04  19,295 4,313 23,608 12,587 12,604 5,047     0 17,842</p>
<p>  Dec 05  19,387 4,323 23,710 12,785 12,805 4,957     0 17,939</p>
<p>  Dec 06  19,385 4,330 23,715 12,892 12,908 4,930     0 17,972</p>
<p>  Dec 09  19,328 4,423 23,751 12,940 12,970 4,707     0 17,963</p>
<p>*A  Of the $19.33 billion in international reserves, $2.77</p>
<p>billion (14.33 percent) are in securities.</p>
<p>*D  There are currently no peso-denominated current</p>
<p>accounts at the Central Bank.</p>
<p>-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +54 1 318-0651</p>
</text>
